<Document>
<name>CERNQ52 Ver005 trajectory and visibility area</name>
<open>1</open>
<description>CERNQ52 Ver005: projected luminous trajectory for the 95% EARLIEST, MEDIAN (weighted mean) and 95% LATEST arrival. Straight line from 90 km to 20 km above the ground, between the points where the estimated gravity-curved path (through the 110 km point -13.684 N, 116.734 E at 2026-09-06 16:06:50.6 UTC) reaches those heights. Speeds are relative to the rotating Earth: 12.25 km/s down to 95 km, then constant deceleration 0.89 km/s^2 (91 g) to 3.0 km/s at 20 km. Luminous path length 73.7 km, duration 9.9 s. Estimated, not observed: the direction comes from the Meerkat e-mail analysis, there is no ablation/fragmentation model, ground taken at the WGS84 ellipsoid. Also shown: the ground area from which the whole trajectory could be seen (green outline) and from which its 90 km top could be seen (yellow outline): observer at sea level, standard refraction, no terrain.</description>
<LookAt><longitude>116.46954</longitude><latitude>-13.74612</latitude><altitude>0</altitude><heading>0</heading><tilt>0</tilt><range>2351021</range><altitudeMode>relativeToGround</altitudeMode></LookAt>
